files_guide='''<p><a href="../START_HERE.html">Back to all packets</a></p><h1>Sample files for SchoolOs testing</h1><p>These files contain invented people. Use them only in the coordinator\'s disposable test school.</p><div class="notice">Do not upload every file into the shared fee baseline. The 30-student list and other upload experiments belong in a separate disposable class or school.</div><h2>Student files</h2><ul><li><a href="students-baseline-six.csv" download>students-baseline-six.csv</a> sets up the six shared students after the three exact classes exist.</li><li><a href="students-names-only.csv" download>students-names-only.csv</a> tests first/last names only, with or without a selected class.</li><li><a href="students-with-classes.csv" download>students-with-classes.csv</a> tests different classes in one file and a blank class. Match the class names/arms to your test school.</li><li><a href="students-invalid.csv" download>students-invalid.csv</a> deliberately contains missing names, duplicate admission numbers and an unknown class. It should fail validation.</li><li><a href="students-leading-zeros.csv" download>students-leading-zeros.csv</a> tests admission number 000123. If editing in Excel, format that column as Text before saving so Excel does not remove the zeros.</li><li><a href="students-pagination-30.csv" download>students-pagination-30.csv</a> tests a default page of 25 students and the remaining five. Select a separate disposable class before uploading.</li></ul><h2>Staff invitations</h2><p><a href="staff-valid-template.csv" download>staff-valid-template.csv</a> needs real controlled test inboxes replacing the example.test addresses before upload. It contains only an email column. Do not send invitations to invented addresses or strangers.</p><p><a href="staff-invalid.csv" download>staff-invalid.csv</a> is deliberately invalid and should not send invitations.</p><h2>Pictures</h2><p><a href="sample-school-logo.png" download>sample-school-logo.png</a> is a small valid PNG for logo/profile-picture checks. <a href="invalid-picture.txt" download>invalid-picture.txt</a> should be rejected as a picture.</p><h2>Helpful reminders</h2><ul><li>Download the selected file, then choose it in the app\'s upload control. A CSV is an Excel-compatible text spreadsheet.</li><li>Use a simple header row and one person per row. Do not use formulas in the upload file.</li><li>If you prefer Excel, open a CSV, keep the column names, and save a copy as Excel Workbook with the xlsx extension. The app accepts xlsx and CSV.</li><li>Names-only files cannot identify the same person reliably across a completely new upload. Include admission numbers when checking for existing records. A saved retry is different: it should not duplicate its original upload.</li><li>Never put passwords or activation codes in the spreadsheet or returned report.</li></ul>'''
(OUT/'sample-files/README.html').write_text(shell('Sample files',files_guide,back='../START_HERE.html'),encoding='utf-8')
coverage='''# SchoolOs manual test coverage

Prepared 2 November 2026. This is a manual test plan, not a record of execution.

The feature packets are written for non-technical users. Platform, outage, time-delay and money tests need a coordinator. Account credentials and real records are deliberately not supplied or created by this document task.

## Implementation sources reviewed

- Frontend app routes, role navigation and dashboard access rules in src/lib/auth/dashboardAccess.ts.
- Shared authentication, Google, invitation, profile and student sign-in screens.
- Student imports and student activation eligibility/code lifecycle.
- Parent dashboard, child-link requests and student-parent request review.
- Attendance roster and owner summaries including optional late/excused states.
- ScoreEntry, marking-scheme locking, release controls and printed reports.
- Exam timetable formats, class groups, published views and A4 export.
- Fee assignments, student balances, family checkout, manual accounts, receipt and report screens.
- Receiving bank verification and its creator/password/code/cooldown rules.
- Published notices, unread tracking, school/own-account settings.
- Offline grants, snapshots, queue handling and PWA preparation.
- Platform school, subscription, team and settings routes/screens.

## Deliberate readiness checks

Visible platform settings/new-school/billing/PIN screens are not assumed production-ready. Test persistence and cross-account behaviour; local-only success or sample rows must not pass. Approval/withdrawal UI must be operable through the app for a full result-release rehearsal. A missing control is outstanding coverage, not a successful skipped test. Public-site editing and grade-scale API configuration are not presented as normal school UI controls in this pack.

## Developer-only checks still needed

These are not tasks for the non-technical testers: tampered tokens, HttpOnly cookie inspection, cross-origin request rules, direct API validation, tenant ID substitution, database/RLS boundary checks, migration/restore/backup drills, rate-limit tuning, payment webhook signatures and replay, provider verification independent of browser return, worker crash/concurrency/lease recovery, email provider failure/retry, and server-side API-only actions not exposed in the UI (including grade-scale and parent-import APIs).

The paired privacy and payment scenarios provide user-level coverage, not a penetration test or replacement for automated server checks. In particular, prepared offline records cannot be remotely erased from a disconnected device; online sync must recheck permission.

Native React Native and Electron projects are foundations and are outside the functional scope of the current web/PWA test. Future native builds need their own install/update/storage/notification/device tests.

## Pack coverage files

feature-coverage.csv maps packets to roles and setup. test-cases.json contains the exact authored case IDs, instructions and expected outcomes for maintaining this pack. assignment-tracker.csv and problem-register.csv are blank working templates, not fabricated reports.
'''
(OUT/'coordinator/IMPLEMENTATION_COVERAGE.md').write_text(coverage,encoding='utf-8')
(OUT/'returned-reports/README.txt').write_text('Put downloaded completed report HTML files, backup JSON files, optional results CSVs and separately named screenshots here.\nThe original feature checklist does not contain a tester\'s saved answers.\nNever store passwords, codes, real card details or complete private invitation/reset links here.\nShare this folder only with authorised reviewers.\n',encoding='utf-8')
(OUT/'READ_ME_FIRST.txt').write_text(f'SchoolOs complete feature testing pack\nPrepared 2 November 2026\n\n{len(PACKS)} assignable feature packets and {TOTAL} numbered test cases.\n\n1. Extract the ZIP folder.\n2. Open START_HERE.html in a web browser.\n3. Coordinators open coordinator/00-coordinator-guide.html first.\n4. Testers open their assigned file in feature-packs.\n5. Download the completed report and backup before returning work.\n\nThe pack runs locally without installing anything or sending answers to SchoolOs. Use a computer for the checklist if a phone cannot open local HTML; you can still test the actual app on the phone. Paper checklists are also printable.\n\nNo live accounts, passwords or database changes were made by creating this pack. Your coordinator must supply controlled test accounts, valid activation codes, the app address and prepared data.\n',encoding='utf-8')
# A flat case checklist is useful for the coordinator without duplicating tester instructions.
